<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Mine</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>mine
mine for &lt;name&gt;
</pre>
<p>Where a seam of iron ore runs through the rock, with a miner's pick 
wielded, you break loose a load of iron ore. There are veins in the 
crystal cavern behind the hobgoblin waterfall and in the hewn passage 
next to it. A vein gives ore once every ten minutes. Mining takes 
endurance, and at low levels it gives a little experience.
</p><p>Sam the blacksmith in Midgaard sells miner's picks (<a cmd='#'>buy pick</a>) and takes 
the ore: give it to him, drop it by him, or unload a cart by him. Each 
load counts for whoever mined it, whoever brings it in, and the 
architect in Midgaard takes it off the price of a lock or a house 
(<a cmd='#'>Help Houses</a>). 
The first load you hand in solves the quest Iron for a Lock.
</p><p><a cmd='#'>mine for &lt;name&gt;</a> mines for a friend: that load counts for them. Ore is 
only taken while whoever mined it is in the game.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Houses</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Fell</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Cart</a>
</pre>




</div>